{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Cap headlight colour temperature as well as brightness to reduce glare",
        "additional_details": "That commissioned research must now be turned into an actual regulatory standard.\r\n\r\nOlder drivers and people with astigmatism can be affected even more severely, as glare sensitivity increases with age \u2014 this problem can only grow as the population ages. In 2016, medical guidance led to a colour temperature cap for street lighting. Headlights sit at eye level and cause more direct, severe glare than streetlights \u2014 any new limit must be set specifically for vehicles, not simply copied from streetlight standards.",
        "background": "We want the Government to cap the maximum colour temperature of vehicle headlights, not just their brightness. The DfT commissioned TRL research confirming headlight glare is a real problem: 96% of drivers surveyed said headlights are too bright & a third have stopped or reduced driving at night. ",
